WEBVTT

00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:03.430
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.400
This is my battle mode, Blue Maiden!

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.360
It's time for us to fight 
together again, Playmaker.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:18.140
Yeah.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:23.470
All the participants are now here.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.570
The enemy is the Light Ignis, Lightning!

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:29.320
In order to save Kusanagi's brother!

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.280
In order to save Miyu!

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.250
And to rebuild Cyberse World!

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:35.990
We will fight!

00:00:54.310 --> 00:01:00.320
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:07.110
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:14.430
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:21.000
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:27.750
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:34.980
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:41.690
I want to share your pain

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:13.620
You gave us quite the trouble, Ignis.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:21.390
In order to collect data, 
we'll now dissect the Ignis.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.890
Stop!  I have free will!

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:27.670
I’m alive!

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:30.960
My memories are vanishing…

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.810
Your name…

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:37.570
Your face…

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:41.490
I can’t… remember…

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:44.950
Now there’s one fewer Ignis.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:50.420
Go Onizuka was missing for a while.  
Why did he go after the Ignis?

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.350
Expanding thought capabilities!

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:57.100
Brain Hack!

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:00.090
An AI has become part of my body.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.460
I have become one with an AI.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:05.440
I can now duel beyond mankind's capabilities.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.200
What Go Onizuka did was foolish.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:13.010
He really wants to become a human-AI hybrid?

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:19.440
Wait.  What's SOL Technologies 
planning to do by acquiring an Ignis?

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.920
This is SOL Technologies’ databank.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.220
Are they serious?

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:03.610
Kengo Dojun aka Blood Shepherd.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:08.730
An AI-hating bounty hunter 
and skilled hacker.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:12.210
He'll be trouble if he becomes our enemy.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:22.110
"Dear Brother,

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:27.130
After seeing the Ignis die, I need to sort my feelings about

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:31.350
what the Ignis are and what I should do.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:34.900
Please let me be alone for a while."

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:36.390
Aoi…

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:40.900
Excuse me, Mr. Zaizen.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:44.600
You have a visitor-

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:52.080
I said no meetings without 
an appointment, but-

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:54.680
I understand.  You can leave.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:55.630
Okay.

00:04:57.810 --> 00:05:00.290
I’m surprised you'd come to me.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:01.660
What do you want?

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:04.410
I need to ask you something.

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:07.930
What is SOL’s true intention?

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:11.500
Are you really trying to kill the Ignis?

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.350
What’s this?

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:22.350
It’s pointless to hide things from me.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:26.220
Using the data you acquired from the Ignis...

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:31.920
...that plan says you plan to create a new 
AI with free will: a high-performance Ignis.

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:37.590
I heard rumors from the researchers, 
but I didn’t know it was true.

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:45.460
If SOL Technologies’ plan is real, your 
superiors hired me under false pretenses.

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:50.240
Even if the Ignis are destroyed, 
a new Ignis will be created!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.690
Seems so.

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:53.240
Seems so?

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:56.240
Zaizen, what do you think about that?

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:01.810
Will you obey your 
company’s actions?  Or…

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:03.420
Don't expect much from me.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:08.040
I’m a lapdog, low level 
in the organization.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:12.560
I can't go against the company’s direction.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.090
You’re lame.

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:18.030
A waste of time to talk to you.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:21.200
I’ll think about what I’ll do.

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:26.540
If he wants to leave SOL, I understand.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:31.840
But I still have my responsibilities, 
even if I'm a lapdog.

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:44.220
Blue Maiden, any regrets?

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:49.080
This fight will be extremely tough.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:52.230
And I dragged you into it.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:56.000
This is no longer just your fight.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:59.980
It's also my fight to rescue Miyu.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:04.540
But you and your brother 
could be on opposing sides.

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:07.540
I’m sure my brother will understand.

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:12.070
Besides, I had to walk 
my own path eventually.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:14.520
It just so happens that time is now.

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:19.220
Over there!

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:24.330
Traces of Lightning’s 
log might still be there!

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:25.690
Okay!  Let’s go!

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:37.370
Well?  Anything left?

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:46.580
No.  No clues at all.

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:51.050
He’s not the type who'd 
carelessly leave clues behind.

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:56.020
Damn!  Not knowing is frustrating!

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:05.270
Ryoken, the Light Ignis and his 
group have gone into hiding.

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:09.970
They plan to act when 
they're perfectly ready.

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:13.060
That'll put us at a disadvantage.

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:19.250
We're doing a thorough search of the 
network to find them ASAP, but...

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:22.720
There’s a way to bring 
them out into the open.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:28.310
But to do that, the Knights 
of Hanoi alone aren't enough.

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:32.190
We need a few more genius programmers.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:34.860
And among the candidates is…

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:39.670
Yes.  Kengo Dojun.  Blood Shepherd.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:47.880
With my missing hand, 
I'll end the other Ignis!

00:08:58.820 --> 00:09:01.090
Until the moment he died...

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:04.090
He was always worried about you.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:11.870
A Knight of Hanoi.

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:17.140
You have a huge hole in your 
heart after losing your father.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:20.870
You know my identity?

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:23.350
There’s nothing I don’t know.

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:29.710
Your desire for revenge didn’t 
vanish with your father’s death.

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:36.920
Your desire for revenge lost its direction, 
growing stronger as you searched for an exit.

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:39.390
Stop talking like you know me!

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:41.430
You know nothing!

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:46.360
Even without your input, I don't 
forgive AIs for harming my mother!

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:47.680
That’s right.

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:50.350
What’s important is 
your desire for revenge.

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:54.480
We - the Hanoi - desire your 
dogged fighting spirit.

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:57.480
We don’t have much time left.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:09:59.110
What are you talking about?

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:03.210
Some of the Ignis have 
declared war against humans.

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:04.040
What?

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:07.010
Now is the time to annihilate the Ignis.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:13.720
Blood Shepherd, don’t you think your 
goal is the same as the Knights of Hanoi?

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:17.270
You’re saying I should team 
up with the Knights of Hanoi?

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:18.700
Yes.

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:27.330
I don't know you guys.  You think 
I'll just blindly join you?

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:32.310
If you can’t abandon your 
pride as a lone wolf...

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:35.810
...I’ll force you to obey me.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:38.810
You’re quite confident.

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:43.790
But I can erase you by the count of three.

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:47.230
One…

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:49.440
Two…

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:56.680
Why at count two?

00:10:56.680 --> 00:11:00.160
You’ll do anything to accomplish your goal.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:03.710
That’s why I chose you.

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:07.600
Interesting.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:11.420
I'm now curious to test the 
Knights of Hanoi's power.

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:21.720
Duel!

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:26.090
I’ll go first.

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:30.800
Fine.  Show me how strong you are.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:32.500
My turn.

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:37.440
I set one card and end my turn.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:40.440
Just one set card?

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:42.910
Are you mocking me?

00:11:43.900 --> 00:11:45.650
You’ll find out.

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:47.660
How dare he.

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:49.630
My turn.  I draw!

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:52.630
I summon Duplicate Drone!

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:57.680
Then Duplicate Drone’s effect from my hand!

00:11:57.680 --> 00:12:01.840
I can Special Summon it when 
there’s another copy on my field.

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:05.180
Appear, Duplicate Drone!

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:09.540
Next, Scud Drone’s effect from my hand!

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:13.680
When there’s a Drone on my 
field, I can Special Summon it!

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:18.920
He already has three monsters.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:22.120
Come out!  The circuit that leads to victory!

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:25.740
Link Summon.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:30.480
Deploy!  Link 2 Battledrone Warrant!

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:35.000
Come out!  The circuit that leads to victory!

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:39.200
The summoning conditions 
are at least two Drones.

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:40.980
Link Summon.

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:45.600
Deploy!  Link 3 Battledrone General!

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:49.850
Due to Battledrone General’s effect...

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:54.420
...I Special Summon a Drone from 
my graveyard next to its link!

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:57.800
Resurrect, Battledrone Warrant!

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:02.590
Battle!  Warrant attacks you directly!

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.270
General’s effect!

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:17.080
When my Drone deals you direct damage, 
I tribute it to activate this effect!

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:20.540
You take damage equal to its ATK!

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:28.400
Regret underestimating me.

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:31.190
This attack will end you!

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:34.440
Battledrone General attacks you directly!

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:37.800
You should calm down a bit.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:39.120
What?

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:41.040
It’s not like you.

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:44.560
Do you think I'll allow that attack?

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:49.770
I activate Checksum Dragon’s 
effect from my hand!

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:55.780
If I took battle damage, if a monster 
attacks me directly that turn...

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:59.450
...I can Special Summon 
this card from my hand!

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:05.400
And I regain LP equal to half its DEF!

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:10.260
In that case, General will 
attack Checksum Dragon!

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:11.960
Go, General!

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:24.340
What?

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.310
Too bad.

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:30.510
When Checksum Dragon is Special 
Summoned because I took damage...

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:33.280
...it can’t be destroyed 
in battle this turn.

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:36.290
I set one card.

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:40.590
I activate the Continuous Spell, 
Blitz Drone, and end my turn.

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:45.830
Battledrone Warrant’s effect 
now activates from my graveyard!

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:50.220
When there are no monsters in the Main 
Monster Zone at the end of the turn...

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:53.770
...it Special Summons 
itself from my graveyard!

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:58.680
I win this duel, Revolver!

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:02.150
I activate the Continuous 
Spell, Blitz Drone’s effect!

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:06.620
By tributing Warrant, you take 1200 damage!

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:08.950
I’m not that easy to beat!

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:13.640
I’ll now show you the power 
of the card you ridiculed!

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.990
That’s the first card you set!

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:20.400
Yes!  I activate the Continuous 
Trap, Imperial Order!

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:28.090
As long as it's in the Spell & Trap Zone, 
all spell cards' effects are negated!

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:29.840
What?

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:35.220
Currently, you won't 
survive against the Ignis.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:39.820
They use fearsome cards known as Link Spells.

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:44.370
I activate the Link Spell, Judgment Arrows!

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:48.870
Appear!  The three arrows 
that judge the world!

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:51.100
Link Spell?

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:54.900
It’s a powerful spell 
card that has Link Markers.

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:56.630
Such a card exists?

00:15:56.630 --> 00:16:01.620
But since it’s a spell 
card, it can be stopped.

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:03.070
Like with this.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:05.810
Why are you telling me?

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:13.780
Since you’re a powerful duelist that 
hates AI, they're likely to attack you.

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:17.200
I don’t want you to be erased.

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:21.430
Help me, Blood Shepherd.

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:23.730
Let's annihilate the Ignis together!

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:25.590
Stop joking!

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:29.200
I walk my own path!  I don’t 
follow anyone’s orders!

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:34.070
His pride as a lone wolf 
won’t allow him to yield.

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:36.170
Oh well.

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:39.200
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:45.500
When Imperial Order is active, I have to 
pay 700 LP at the beginning of the turn.

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:48.150
When there’s a Link 
Monster on your field...

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:51.900
...I can Special Summon 
Gateway Dragon from my hand!

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:56.830
Gateway Dragon’s effect activates!

00:16:56.830 --> 00:17:02.220
I Special Summon a Level 4 or 
lower Dark Dragon from my hand!

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:05.530
Come out, DMZ Dragon!

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:11.410
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:15.580
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Effect Monsters!

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:23.530
I set Gateway, Checksum and DMZ 
Dragons in the Link Markers!

00:17:23.530 --> 00:17:30.370
Appear, Link 3 Topologic Trisbaena!

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:40.140
I activate the Continuous Trap, 
Capture Drone on Trisbaena!

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:42.600
As long as this card exists...

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:46.620
...the target monster can’t attack, has its effects

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:49.380
negated and can’t be tributed to Link Summon!

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:53.850
Your monster has been completely sealed away!

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:58.360
That’s not enough to tie me down.

00:17:58.360 --> 00:18:03.910
As long as there’s a monster on your 
field, and there’s a Link Monster on my field...

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:06.960
...I can Special Summon 
this card from my hand.

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:09.820
Come out, Vulnerability Dragon!

00:18:11.670 --> 00:18:15.620
When it’s Special Summoned 
due to this effect...

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:21.880
...I must destroy one of my monsters 
for every monster on your field.

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:25.390
I destroy Topologic Trisbaena!

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:30.310
What?  You destroyed your own ace monster?

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:33.800
Capture Drone lost its 
target, so it’s destroyed.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:39.040
Now my Link Monster can attack.

00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:41.510
That's what you were aiming for.

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:43.280
Let me show you.

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:47.490
I summon the Tuner Monster, Rokket Synchron!

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:52.720
Tuner Monster?

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:55.550
Rokket Synchron’s effect activates!

00:18:55.550 --> 00:19:00.370
When it's summoned, I Special Summon a Level 5 or

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:04.560
higher Dragon from my graveyard in defense position!

00:19:04.630 --> 00:19:07.760
Resurrect, Checksum Dragon!

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:21.240
Level 1 Rokket Synchron tunes Level 1 
Vulnerability Dragon and Level 6 Checksum Dragon!

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:28.150
Heroic dragon!

00:19:28.150 --> 00:19:32.360
Fire by transforming your 
ferocious fangs into bullets!

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:33.900
Synchro Summon!

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:38.230
Come out, Level 8!

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:44.040
Borreload Savage Dragon!

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:48.140
You had another ace monster!

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:51.600
Borreload Savage Dragon’s effect activates!

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:54.610
When it's Synchro Summoned...

00:19:54.610 --> 00:20:00.250
...a Link Monster in the graveyard is treated 
as an Equip Card and equipped on to this card.

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:04.480
And gains a Borrel Counter for 
every one of its Link Markers!

00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:07.720
I equip Trisbaena!

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:21.170
And it gains half the equipped monster's ATK.

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:24.420
Battle!

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:30.860
Borreload Savage Dragon 
attacks Battledrone General!

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:44.640
I banish DMZ Dragon from my 
graveyard to activate its effect!

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:50.600
By destroying the battling monster's 
Equip Card, it can attack again!

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:52.570
Consecutive attacks?

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:58.570
Since it no longer equips a monster, 
Savage Dragon’s ATK return to normal.

00:21:00.550 --> 00:21:04.800
Borreload Savage Dragon attacks you directly!

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:21.550
So this is the power of the Hanoi.

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:24.530
The rebel Ignis are powerful.

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:30.080
In your current state, you can't 
win against their Link Spells.

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:33.020
Use this duel as a lesson.

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:36.680
I don’t need your advice!

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:38.000
I'll pay you back!

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:41.460
I heard you’re the type 
who hates being in debt.

00:21:42.680 --> 00:21:46.400
It means you’re that 
special of an opponent.

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:49.820
I promise to pay this back someday.

00:21:50.890 --> 00:21:56.370
The lone wolf that wanders the 
wastelands - Blood Shepherd.

